  "prefLabel": "Per 102.59 Minor group",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Per 102.59 “Minor group” means a subdivision of a major group that contains job titles within a more specific occupational area grouped together on the basis of similar skills, education, training, and credentials, and which aligns with the national Standard Occupational Classification (SOC) System’s use of the same term.\n\nSource. #13667, eff 6-22-23; renumbered by #14065-A; renumbered by #14132-A; ss by #14434 (formerly Per 102.51), eff 12-1-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/per100-1500.html"
